      "content": "i get that scholars have different views now, but it feels like you're saying the \"pro-deregulation\" side was basically just a misunderstanding that's been debunked. isn't it a bit of a stretch to say it wasn't a driver of growth? like, isn't it pretty objectively true that removing those barriers led to much higher market efficiency and competition? i'm trying to figure out if there's actually a balanced debate here or if the \"deregulation = bad\" side is just the modern standard.",
